as the horror genre's reigning final  girl lori strode played by jamie lee  curtis exceeds her reputation in the  2018 sequel halloween despite the  self-inflicted isolation of her  militaristic lifestyle and the resulting  strained relationships with her family  strode is ready for the inevitable  return of michael myers halloween is the  first installment in a trilogy directed  by david gordon green the films are  direct sequels to the original 1978 film  of the same name directed by john  carpenter the film became the highest  grossing entry in the halloween  franchise making over 250 million  dollars worldwide according to  entertainment weekly co-writer danny  mcbride said they were eager to shoot a  sequel but wanted to make sure audiences  were on board first halloween is  certified fresh on rotten tomatoes with  many critics and fans agreeing that it's  a welcome change for the franchise now  the much anticipated sequel halloween  kills is officially on the horizon and  here's everything we know about the film  so far the initial release date of  halloween kills was october 16 2020 but  a july 2020 statement from green and  carpenter revealed that the film was  delayed because of the pandemic not  dissimilar to many other films that were  scheduled to be released in 2020. if we  release it in october of this year as  planned we have to face the reality that  the film would be consumed in a  compromised theatrical experience after  weighing our options we have chosen to  push the film's theatrical release by  one year now nearly one year later  halloween kills is scheduled to premiere  at the 17th venice international film  festival on september 8th it'll be  hitting u.s theaters on october 15th  additionally the release date for  halloween ends is set for october 14th  2022 meaning we shouldn't have to endure  such a brutal wait time before seeing  the trilogy's final entry of course  jamie lee curtis will be reprising her  iconic role as lori strode the tormented  babysitter turned fighter the other  strode women will be returning as well  judy greer is back as laurie's estranged  daughter karen and andy matichak is back  as karen's daughter allison additionally  michael myers will be portrayed by nick  castle and james jude courtney again  will patton and jabril natambu will also  be reprising their roles from the  previous film while halloween kills is  naturally pulling from characters  introduced in the 2018 film it's also  bringing back characters from the 1978  version the young children laurie  babysat in the original are all grown up  now tommy doyle will be portrayed by  anthony michael hall while kyle richards  is reprising her role as lindsay wallace  nancy stevens is reprising her role as  marion chambers a retired nurse charles  ciphers is reprising his role as lee  bracket the former haddenfield sheriff  whose daughter was killed by myers in an  interview with empire green and mcbride  explained that halloween kills picks up  directly where the previous film ended  however while the first film focused on  lori's life 40 years after surviving a  brutal killing spree green said this is  more about the unraveling of a community  into chaos the 2018 film ends with  michael myers trapped and left for dead  in lori's flame engulfed home but as  fans know the captain kirk masked killer  doesn't go down easily or at all the  halloween kills trailer shows myers  walking out to the front door and  attacking the firefighters before  resuming his reign of terror on the  small midwestern town as myers leaves a  trail of bodies leading to his childhood  home where it all began the haddenfield  residents rallied together to hunt down  the obsessive killer lori leaves the  hospital where she's recovering from a  stab wound and makes a bold declaration  evil  dies  tonight mcbride explained to empire  events in the film bring together a lot  of characters who were in the 1978 film  who we didn't see last time they gather  to try once and for all to take down  michael to stop this madman it's  unlikely that myers will be defeated in  halloween kills especially considering  that there's one more film to come in  the trilogy but anything's possible  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

